t:EffectiveDateOfReasonOfChange><in-capmkt:BriefProfile contextRef="D_ChangeInManagement1">Siddharth Purandare brings over 23 years of experience in the financial services industry, with a career spanning business leadership, credit risk, sales strategy and product innovation across diverse lending segments. He has consistently played a lead role in building and scaling lending businesses from the ground up, bringing deep expertise in retail lending operations, credit risk management and co-lending partnerships with banks and financial institutions.
Siddharth was instrumental in setting up an MSME-focused NBFC in India for US-based AVANA Companies, leading the venture from incorporation through regulatory approval, board formation and technology &amp; AI infrastructure build-out, while also contributing to the group's market entry into Saudi Arabia through Shariah-compliant product design.
Prior to this, he spent over a decade at Edelweiss Retail Finance Limited, rising through progressively senior roles across sales leadership and credit risk to ultimately head Credit Risk nationally for SME Lending, where he built underwriting infrastructure across multiple regions and played a key role in the industry-wide rollout of government-backed MSME credit schemes.
This diversified experience across lending segments, credit cycles and geographies gives Siddharth a macro-level perspective of the broader lending market — an asset he now brings to Company as CEO in shaping its strategic direction, driving profitable growth, sound governance and technology-led transformation, with a continued focus on scaling the portfolio through disciplined execution and strong institutional partnerships.
Siddharth holds an M.M.S. (Finance) from the Jamnalal Bajaj Institute of Management Studies (JBIMS), Mumbai University, and a Bachelor's degree in Mechanical Engineering from Fr. Agnel, Mumbai University.
